meta {
  name: Verify Join Request Code
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/auth/email-code/join-request/verify
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}
}

body:json {
  "challengeId": "REPLACE_WITH_CHALLENGE_ID",
  "code": "123456",
  "name": "Ada",
  "message": "I'd love to join, a friend in the network told me about it.",
  "heardFrom": "A friend",
  "ageAttested": true,
  "termsVersion": "1.0"
}

docs {
  Step two (SEC-10): the form plus the code from "Request Join Request
  Code", sent from the same client so the email_code_requester cookie rides
  along. The request is filed under the address the code went to, so the body
  carries no email. 201 returns { id, status, createdAt, statusToken } once.
  A wrong code answers 400 code_incorrect; 403 REAPPLICATION_COOLDOWN and
  409 JOIN_REQUEST_PENDING come only after a correct code.
}
